menu "Bicopter sensor hardware"

    config BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        bool "Physical IMU/barometer sensors are wired to this board"
        default n
        help
            No ESP32 board/pinout has been finalized for this project yet (see docs/hardware.md).
            Leave disabled until a board is chosen and the I2C pins below are set to match it -
            SensorTask (firmware/main/sensor_task.c) gracefully skips real sensor I2C init/reads
            while this is disabled, logging a stub reading instead of attempting a bus that
            doesn't exist. Flip this on and fill in the pins below once a board with an MPU6050
            and BMP581 wired up exists.

    config BICOPTER_I2C_PORT
        int "I2C port number"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 0

    config BICOPTER_I2C_SDA_GPIO
        int "I2C SDA GPIO"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 21
        help
            Placeholder default (ESP32's commonly-used default I2C SDA pin) - not verified against
            any actual board wiring. Set to match the real board once one is chosen.

    config BICOPTER_I2C_SCL_GPIO
        int "I2C SCL GPIO"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 22
        help
            Placeholder default (ESP32's commonly-used default I2C SCL pin) - not verified against
            any actual board wiring. Set to match the real board once one is chosen.

    config BICOPTER_I2C_CLOCK_HZ
        int "I2C clock speed (Hz)"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default 400000
        help
            400kHz ("fast mode") - both the MPU6050 and BMP581 support it per their datasheets.

    config BICOPTER_MPU6050_INT_GPIO
        int "MPU6050 data-ready interrupt GPIO (-1 disables, falls back to polling)"
        depends on BICOPTER_SENSORS_ENABLED
        default -1
        help
            See firmware/components/sensors/include/mpu6050.h - GPIO_NUM_NC (-1) makes
            mpu6050_read() poll the INT_STATUS data-ready bit each call instead of blocking on an
            interrupt-fed queue. Set to a real GPIO once the MPU6050's INT pin is wired to one.

endmenu

menu "Bicopter radio (ESP-NOW)"

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        bool "ESP-NOW radio link is paired with a ground-station peer"
        default n
        help
            No ground-station peer has been paired or tested in this environment yet (no physical
            hardware - see docs/radio.md). Leave disabled until a peer MAC is configured below and
            two real ESP32 boards are available to pair. RadioTask (firmware/main/radio_task.c)
            gracefully skips Wi-Fi/ESP-NOW init while this is disabled, logging a stub cadence
            instead of bringing up a radio link that has nothing to talk to.

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_PEER_MAC
        string "Paired peer MAC address (AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF)"
        depends on BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        default "FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF"
        help
            Placeholder broadcast address - replace with the ground-station peer's real MAC once
            one is chosen and paired. See docs/radio.md's pairing procedure.

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_WIFI_CHANNEL
        int "Wi-Fi channel"
        depends on BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 1
        help
            Both peers must be set to the same fixed channel - ESP-NOW rides on the Wi-Fi radio
            without an actual AP association/channel negotiation. Valid range 1-13
            (region-dependent).

    config BICOPTER_RADIO_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Command staleness timeout (ms)"
        depends on BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 500
        help
            has_command()/get_health().link_alive (firmware/components/radio/include/radio.h)
            report the link lost if no valid command packet is received within this window. 500ms
            is a placeholder, 10x RadioTask's own 20ms/50Hz cycle - see docs/radio.md. The actual
            failsafe *behavior* once the link is considered lost is Milestone 16's job, not this
            option's.

endmenu

menu "Bicopter radio (CRSF RC receiver)"

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        bool "CRSF RC receiver is wired to this board"
        default n
        help
            No RC receiver has been wired or tested in this environment yet (no physical hardware
            - see docs/radio.md). Leave disabled until a receiver is connected to the UART pins
            below. RadioTask (firmware/main/radio_task.c) gracefully skips UART/CRSF init while
            this is disabled, logging a stub cadence instead. Mutually exclusive with
            BICOPTER_RADIO_ENABLED (ESP-NOW): enabling both is a build-time error in
            radio_task.c, since only one radio transport backs RadioTask's single radio_t at a
            time until a real board decides otherwise (Milestone 17).

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_UART_PORT
        int "UART port number"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 1
        help
            UART0 is typically reserved for the console/programming interface on most ESP32 dev
            boards - UART1 is a safer placeholder default. Set to match the real board once one is
            chosen.

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_UART_RX_GPIO
        int "CRSF UART RX GPIO (receiver TX wire connects here)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 16
        help
            Placeholder default, not verified against any actual board wiring - see
            docs/hardware.md.

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_UART_TX_GPIO
        int "CRSF UART TX GPIO (-1 disables; unused this milestone)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default -1
        help
            CRSF telemetry write-back (this device -> RC receiver -> transmitter) is out of scope
            for Milestone 15 - see docs/radio.md. Left configurable for whenever that follow-up
            lands; -1 leaves the TX pin unconfigured (UART_PIN_NO_CHANGE).

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_BAUD_RATE
        int "CRSF UART baud rate"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 420000
        help
            420000 is CRSF's common default; some receiver/transmitter pairs use 400000, 921600,
            or higher - configurable, not hardcoded to one vendor's convention.

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Command staleness timeout (ms)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 200
        help
            has_command()/get_health().link_alive report the link lost if no valid RC_CHANNELS
            frame is received within this window. CRSF links commonly run well under 20ms/frame,
            so 200ms is a shorter placeholder than ESP-NOW's 500ms default - still a placeholder
            pending real hardware measurement (Milestone 17), and still not what happens once the
            link is lost, which is Milestone 16's job.

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_NOMINAL_FRAME_PERIOD_US
        int "Nominal frame period (microseconds), for the packet-loss estimate"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 4000
        help
            CRSF carries no sequence number (unlike this project's own ESP-NOW packet format), so
            radio_health_t.packet_loss_percent is estimated from elapsed time against this
            configured nominal period rather than counted from sequence-number gaps - see
            docs/radio.md. Set to roughly match the transmitter's real configured CRSF update rate
            once known; a wrong value only makes this figure meaningless, it never affects
            link_alive/staleness detection.

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_THROTTLE_CHANNEL
        int "Throttle channel index (0-15)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 0

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_ROLL_CHANNEL
        int "Roll channel index (0-15)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 1

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_PITCH_CHANNEL
        int "Pitch channel index (0-15)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 2

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_YAW_CHANNEL
        int "Yaw channel index (0-15)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 3

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_ARM_CHANNEL
        int "Arm-switch channel index (0-15)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 4

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_FLIGHT_MODE_CHANNEL
        int "Flight-mode-switch channel index (0-15)"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 5

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_FLIGHT_MODE_POSITIONS
        int "Flight-mode switch position count"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 3
        help
            Number of discrete positions to quantize the flight-mode channel into (e.g. 3 for a
            standard 3-position switch). flight_mode is reported as 0..(positions-1).

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_RAW_MIN
        int "Raw channel value at the low endpoint"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 172
        help
            172/992/1811 are the de facto CRSF/OpenTX endpoint convention (~988-2012us mapped onto
            an 11-bit raw range) - a reasonable default, not this project asserting it's correct
            for every transmitter. Measure and set the real endpoints for the actual TX/RX pair
            once hardware exists - see docs/radio.md's calibration procedure.

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_RAW_CENTER
        int "Raw channel value at center/neutral"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 992

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_RAW_MAX
        int "Raw channel value at the high endpoint"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 1811

    config BICOPTER_CRSF_ARM_THRESHOLD
        int "Raw channel value at/above which the arm channel reads as armed"
        depends on BICOPTER_CRSF_RADIO_ENABLED
        default 992

endmenu

menu "Bicopter battery monitoring"

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        bool "Battery voltage-divider (and optional current-sense) ADC is wired to this board"
        default n
        help
            No battery/voltage-divider hardware has been chosen or wired to this board yet (see
            docs/hardware.md's "Battery cell count / voltage-divider and current-sense scaling:
            TBD" entry). Leave disabled until a divider is built and the ADC channel/ratio below
            are set to match it - SafetyTask (firmware/main/safety_task.c) gracefully skips real
            ADC init/reads while this is disabled. The arming precondition battery_ok fails closed
            (reports false, blocking arming) while this is disabled, same as imu_valid/
            radio_link_alive do when their own hardware/link is absent - a missing signal is never
            treated as "ok," see docs/safety.md.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_ADC_UNIT
        int "ADC unit (1 or 2)"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default 1
        help
            ESP32 has two SAR ADC units; ADC2 is shared with Wi-Fi and unusable while Wi-Fi is
            active (relevant if ESP-NOW radio is also enabled - see docs/radio.md). Unit 1 is the
            safer default for a board that may also use ESP-NOW.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_VOLTAGE_ADC_CHANNEL
        int "Voltage-sense ADC channel"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default 0
        help
            Placeholder default, not verified against any actual board wiring - see
            docs/hardware.md.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_ADC_ATTENUATION
        int "ADC attenuation (0=0dB, 1=2.5dB, 2=6dB, 3=12dB)"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default 3
        help
            12dB attenuation gives the ESP32's widest input range (~0-3.1V), the usual choice
            downstream of a voltage divider sized to keep Vadc within that range at the pack's
            maximum voltage.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_VOLTAGE_DIVIDER_RATIO_MILLI
        int "Voltage-divider ratio (Vbat/Vadc), x1000"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default 11000
        help
            Placeholder (11.000:1), not derived from any chosen resistor pair - see
            docs/hardware.md's TBD entry and docs/safety.md. Vbat = Vadc * (this value / 1000).
            Set to match the real divider once built: ratio = (R1+R2)/R2 for a divider with R1
            from Vbat to the ADC pin and R2 from the ADC pin to ground.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_CELL_COUNT
        int "Battery cell count (S)"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default 3
        help
            Scales the per-cell LOW/CRITICAL thresholds below and the default percentage curve
            (battery_default_single_cell_curve() in battery_convert.c) to the configured pack.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_LOW_VOLTAGE_PER_CELL_MV
        int "LOW_BATTERY threshold, millivolts per cell"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default 3500
        help
            A common conservative LiPo per-cell "getting low" rest-voltage figure - not derived
            from any specific cell's datasheet. See docs/safety.md for the full battery-monitoring
            caveat. Multiplied by BICOPTER_BATTERY_CELL_COUNT to get the pack-level threshold.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_CRITICAL_VOLTAGE_PER_CELL_MV
        int "CRITICAL_BATTERY threshold, millivolts per cell"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default 3300
        help
            A common conservative LiPo per-cell "must land now" rest-voltage figure - not derived
            from any specific cell's datasheet, and does not account for load-sag (see
            docs/safety.md). Multiplied by BICOPTER_BATTERY_CELL_COUNT to get the pack-level
            threshold.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_CURRENT_SENSE_ENABLED
        bool "Current-sense ADC channel is also wired (optional - see docs/safety.md)"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Voltage monitoring is this milestone's priority; current sensing is supported (a
            second ADC channel through the same linear-scaling conversion path) but not required -
            see AGENTS.md/docs/safety.md. No current-sense shunt/hall-sensor hardware is chosen
            yet.

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_CURRENT_ADC_CHANNEL
        int "Current-sense ADC channel"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_CURRENT_SENSE_ENABLED
        default 1

    config BICOPTER_BATTERY_CURRENT_SCALE_MILLIAMPS_PER_VOLT
        int "Current-sense scale, milliamps per volt at the ADC pin"
        depends on BICOPTER_BATTERY_CURRENT_SENSE_ENABLED
        default 40000
        help
            Placeholder (40A/V), not derived from any chosen shunt/hall-sensor part - depends
            entirely on the current-sense hardware eventually chosen (see docs/hardware.md).

endmenu

menu "Bicopter safety / failsafe thresholds"

    config BICOPTER_SAFETY_MAX_TILT_ANGLE_DEG
        int "Maximum tilt-from-level before EXCESSIVE_ATTITUDE failsafe triggers (degrees, 0=disabled)"
        default 60
        help
            Placeholder, not tuned against any real flight envelope (no hardware exists yet - see
            docs/hardware.md). See docs/safety.md. This check cannot currently fire in firmware -
            no estimator runs in firmware yet to supply a real tilt angle (see docs/safety.md's
            "What's wired to live data, and what isn't yet" section) - but is implemented, real,
            and host-tested (failsafe.c / tests/failsafe_test.c), ready for when that wiring lands.

    config BICOPTER_SAFETY_MAX_ANGULAR_RATE_DPS
        int "Maximum body angular rate before EXCESSIVE_ANGULAR_VELOCITY failsafe triggers (deg/s, 0=disabled)"
        default 500
        help
            Placeholder, not tuned against any real flight envelope. Unlike the tilt-angle check
            above, this one DOES have a real firmware signal source: SafetyTask peeks the raw gyro
            rate from SensorTask's sample queue (see docs/safety.md) - no estimator dependency.

    config BICOPTER_SAFETY_STATIONARY_MAX_ANGULAR_RATE_DPS
        int "Maximum body angular rate to consider the vehicle stationary for arming (deg/s, 0=disabled)"
        default 20
        help
            Part of the arming precondition set (arming.h's arming_is_stationary()) - the design
            brief's explicit "check the vehicle is stationary during arming" requirement. Real
            firmware signal source: the same raw gyro peek as the angular-rate failsafe above.

    config BICOPTER_ALTITUDE_HOLD_ENABLED
        bool "Enable the experimental ALTITUDE_HOLD flight mode"
        default n
        help
            ALTITUDE_HOLD is explicitly experimental and disabled/unreachable by default per this
            project's design brief - no barometer-based altitude/vertical-velocity estimator
            exists yet (docs/estimation.md notes this is deferred), so ALTITUDE_HOLD has no real
            control loop behind it even when this gate is enabled. See docs/safety.md. Requesting
            ALTITUDE_HOLD from the radio while this is off is a documented no-op in
            flight_mode.c, not an error.

endmenu
